WEBVTT

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.950
They're here!

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:06.620
Good morning.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:07.120
Good morning.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.420
Good morning!

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.260
Jeez, don't scream beside my ear!

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.960
That's my trademark!

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.060
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:14.960
Good morning.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.960
Yo! Good morning.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.600
You're in the semifinals!

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.430
Congratulations!

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.430
Thanks!

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.170
How did you guys know?

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.340
Gouda-kun and the others went to see the match!

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.970
You haven't scored yet.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.910
How about you, Erika-chan?

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:28.940
Yeah!

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:29.810
Wow!

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.250
I'm a defender so I can't score that easily.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.950
But I'll score when needed!

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.220
That won't come in a long time.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.620
Erika-chan!

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.220
When's the next match?

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.560
Next Sunday.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.690
We'll go and cheer you on again.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.360
Really?

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.390
I'll go, too!

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:48.090
Really?

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:48.990
Me, too!

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.030
I'm so happy!

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.230
You're all very welcome!

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.000
I think everyone will be happy!

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.600
These girls have something to ask you.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.840
What is it?

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.880
Yes... U-Um...

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.580
Don't push me!

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.150
Um... We saw the match yesterday...

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.020
Really?

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.720
I was so touched that you were able to beat such an amazing team!

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.920
Really?

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.860
It was amazing!

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.290
You were so cool!

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.930
No way...

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.430
We'll come see you again!

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.900
Please keep on winning!

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.930
Thank you.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:28.900
I'll do my best.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.100
Um, Outa-kun...

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.270
Here!

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.510
Eh!?

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.710
Attack of the presents!?

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.380
I'm so popular all of a sudden!

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.650
Please give this to Kota-san!

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.820
Give this to Ryuuji-san!

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.660
Please give this to Ouzou-san!

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.720
What are these?

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.820
From your fans.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:33.260
I don't want it.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.360
Why don't you hold onto that for me?

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.560
Mine, too.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.070
There's no way I'm keeping your presents!{How can I take your presents? }

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.070
I gave them to you. Got it!?

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.240
What's with him?

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.440
Dunno.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.280
Hey!

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.510
Coach Hanashima left us a message.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:55.980
He wants us to practice by ourselves today since he has something to do.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.080
Something to do?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:01.790
Something about meeting someone from his old team.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:07.990
Well, since the coach isn't here today, let's just do some light practice and head home early.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.060
No way!

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.500
We need to do our best here!

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.000
Really?

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.670
We gotta do what the captain says.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.470
Tch.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.080
Ryuuji, what's wrong?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.920
It's time for running.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.650
Okay. I'll be right there.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.760
Okay! Momoyama Predators! Fight!

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.130
Oh!

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:52.640
This is the own goal from Ouzou's play.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:58.080
Masaru-chan-san, what do you think about this as a coach?

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.080
Eh?

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.450
They did those two plays on purpose, right?{Do you think they did this on purpose? }

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.450
The own goal, too?

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.020
I'm here.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.720
Excuse me.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:48.090
Thanks for coming.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.760
Long time no see.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:54.000
It's been so long that I was a bit surprised when I got your message.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.370
You seem to be doing well. That's good.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.540
Thanks.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.780
It's nice that you've taken up soccer again.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:08.280
Must be tough getting away from it all after relying on soccer for your meals for so long. {Must be tough getting away from it all after working for so long. }

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.920
Is black coffee all right with you?

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.550
Thanks.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:16.790
I'd rather be the coach of some team instead of rotting away here.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:20.660
My body doesn't listen to me well anymore.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:24.060
I've heard that a lot.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:27.030
It was terrible back then.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.270
The Bolts finally got promoted to J1.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:33.110
You got injured and had to retire.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.910
You were even called up to the national team.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.010
That's the past now.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:47.390
When I got back I heard that you quit being the coach of an elementary school team.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:50.890
Yes.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.420
Don't make that face.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.160
You make it seem like I did something bad.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:55.660
Eh?

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.660
You were sent to the hospital,

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:01.270
but I never thought that you would retire.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:05.240
After a hit like that? It was inevitable.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:06.610
What are you saying?

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.540
We would have kept playing you.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.010
We had huge expectations of you.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.350
Really?

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.980
Hey, hey, don't doubt me here.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.490
How nostalgic.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:23.490
Yeah.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:27.890
Your skills in front of goal weren't anything special, but the team needed them.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:30.660
Your off-the-ball play was quite bad in the beginning, too.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.970
But it got much better.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:36.500
In any case, your long distance shooting was amazing.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:40.140
As long as you were on the pitch, the opposing team got so scared.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:46.180
I think your shooting foot can still be the key to the national team.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:49.950
It would have been nice of you to say that when you were still working.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:51.580
I couldn't say that.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.720
Your pace got slower and slower.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.990
Soccer is said to be a game between a king and ten servants.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.690
I know.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:03.260
The king wasn't me.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:06.900
That's right. The king is the one with the ball.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.800
The remaining ten players sweat for his sake.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:10.670
Also...

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:13.410
Defend with ten, attack with eight.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.340
You remembered!

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.880
If the forwards come back to defend, it'll be hard to attack.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.210
I heard that from you a lot when you were still working.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.180
But you kept thinking the opposite inside your head.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.350
Really?

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:28.020
You bastard.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.890
So why are you here today? Not to reminisce about the past, right?

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.130
Can I borrow that DVD player over there?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.570
This was from our first match.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:48.670
Which one is your team?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.710
The one with red stripes.{Our team has red stripes. }

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:06.930
That's fast. They scored already?

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.390
They are the triplets I talked about over the phone.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:13.130
Their skills are far beyond the remaining players.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.930
Did you win by a large margin?

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.400
From the results, yes.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:22.240
But it became dango soccer and we went into the second half with the score tied.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.240
I see.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:28.410
The triplets weren't happy with the starting formation and the team got tangled up.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:32.380
That's just like our team in the past.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:37.220
Please look at the next scene.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:42.960
What's going on here?

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.380
He ran backwards to create space?

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:03.680
That surprised them.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:06.750
The defense is having problems.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:08.990
Oh?

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:11.360
That girl is great!

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:12.960
She took the ball cleanly!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.190
She's fast, too.

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:17.230
Oh, nice pass.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.630
Yes!

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:24.170
That was a fabulous goal.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:29.310
The assist was amazing, too. Good job.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.680
Stop!

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:32.410
Pass me the remote.{Let me see the remote. }

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.020
Own goal?

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.630
Hey, hey, hey.

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:51.960
If you nurture the three of them properly, they'll become monsters!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.600
Nurture them properly, huh?

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:56.470
That's the problem.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.670
Oh, that guy's very hotblooded.

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:06.440
We were down 0-2 at the end of first half here,

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:10.750
but we turned the tables in the second half using three tactics.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:24.160
Huh? Another own goal?

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:36.580
Hey, this...

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:38.940
There's one more match.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:57.230
If I was the ref, that would have been a yellow card.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:00.870
There's no rule against creating own goals.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:04.740
Think about what the kids of the opposing team would feel.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.410
"Why did the ball come to me like that?"

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:11.780
I was thinking about what you would say.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:17.780
Hey, hey. I've never seen such a weak Lightning Light.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:21.750
I've dealt with a problematic player in our team, too.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:25.490
A forward with a twisted personality.

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:30.430
He only thought about shooting and never bothered to defend.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:35.600
Even if he had no shooting course, he 
would punt the ball straight at the defense.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:39.270
A twisted coach nurtures twisted players.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:43.510
I have nothing to offer you. Just deal with it yourself.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:46.080
I don't really understand this myself.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:50.980
If they have such great skill, why 
would they aim for an own goal?

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:56.390
I had a twisted personality, but I think I was more simple.

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:59.390
Don't say that yourself.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.990
I do have something to say, though.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.900
You won't conquer the nation with this team.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:10.970
Your last team, Miyakogawa, was a better team.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:14.870
The city tournament will probably be your limit here.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.210
The skill level this year is quite high.

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:19.880
What do you mean?

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.810
You're aiming for New Tokyo FC, right?

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:25.620
Not that! What is the problem with our team!?

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.120
You already know the answer yourself, right?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.460
You rely on the triplets too much.

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:35.090
They act like they're the kings even without the ball.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:38.530
The center back does give orders on what tactic to use,

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:41.600
but that won't work at the national level .

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:44.970
There's only one answer. Team play.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.180
I remembered this from watching the DVD.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.810
You've seen this before, right?

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:58.350
The team with Johan Cruyff on it?

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:01.420
The game in which they defeated Brazil was amazing.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:04.290
After that game, the world of soccer changed.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.030
This game doesn't feel that old still, right?

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:11.530
If you follow what the Netherlands did and played total soccer,

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.000
your team will get stronger.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:18.140
Thank you for taking the time to chat with me.

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:19.700
Oh? You going already?

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:20.770
Yes.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:21.940
I see.

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:24.180
Please swing by the practice grounds before you leave.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:24.880
Huh?

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:25.880
Okay?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.780
All right. Later.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.920
I'll come see your matches if I have time.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:43.030
What are they wearing on their heads?

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:45.600
Eh? Is that Hanashima-san?

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.570
Hello! Long time no see!

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.240
I had something to do here. What kind of practice are they doing?

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.710
That? Blind soccer.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.310
Blind soccer?

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:59.340
You don't know? It's soccer for people with eye problems.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.410
Eye problems!?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.620
45 degrees to the right! Kuma-chan is free!

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:08.220
Go!

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:10.790
The goal's to the left! Right there! Right there!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.060
Can they really not see!?

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:20.230
They have a towel around their heads behind the eyepatch.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.330
Wow.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.300
Yeah.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.240
Like that!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.310
How can he pull off a roulette when he can't see?

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:32.880
That's our ace. He's just a high school student.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:33.950
His name is...

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.630
Give the ball to Youhei!

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:54.100
Don't leave the front of goal!

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.130
Okay!

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.470
Your off-the-ball play is the keystone to our team!

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.170
Don't lose!

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.310
Youhei!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:11.550
I'm really sorry, but there are long term problems.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:15.220
No way... Youhei!

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:21.530
What am I thinking? That can't be Youhei.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.970
Are you leaving already, Hanashima-san?

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:27.830
Yes.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:31.070
Hanashima-san.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:40.410
Coach! Long time no see! You're over there, right?

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:43.780
I'm Youhei. Kuribayashi Youhei.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.120
Eh? Are you there?

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:52.990
He is. He's just a bit shocked.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.830
Y-You've gotten bigger.

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:58.560
That's the voice! I haven't heard that in a while!

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:01.870
You're mistaken. I haven't changed at all.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.340
Have you gotten fatter?

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:05.770
You can see!?

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:08.740
Just a thought. Were you surprised?

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:11.440
I can actually see a little now.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:12.440
Really?

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:15.580
Well, normal soccer is a bit tough.

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:17.150
I see.

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:21.850
But that's great. Just great.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:26.930
Nagabuchi-san told me yesterday that you'll be here today.

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:30.630
I've been invited to the training camp for the national team!

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:33.000
This is all thanks to your strict coaching.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.830
No, I...

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.970
I see. Congratulations.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.370
That's great!

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:42.110
You didn't give up on soccer.

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:43.680
Thank goodness.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.780
That's my line.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:49.680
I couldn't contact you at all after the accident. I was really worried.

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:55.550
But when I heard that you started coaching a youth team again, I was really relieved.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:59.190
It's great. Really great.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.730
I'll come see your match next time.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.570
Thank you very much.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:12.400
Let's play a game next time. I won't lose to you.

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:16.110
You've gotten cocky. Later!

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:09.030
Where are the others?

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:11.230
They went home after practice.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:14.330
It's rare to see you stay behind.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:16.500
I was waiting for you to come back, Coach.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:17.340
Me?

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:21.510
What?

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:26.340
Your face used to be all tensed up, but now you're all relaxed.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:27.980
Forget about me.

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:29.850
Something looks wrong with you, though.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.520
You talked with our father, right?

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:41.660
People say he's a strange person, but please forgive him.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.460
You must have heard, right?

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:46.930
What?

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.370
About me.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:51.000
I couldn't believe it at first.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.370
But after watching it so many times, I'm forced to believe it.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:57.180
Our last coach got so mad.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:20:01.350
But we scored. What's so wrong about that?

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:06.020
The other team gets a huge shock, too.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:08.820
But that coach told us to stop.

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.220
That's what some people think.

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:15.730
The referees will not look kindly on Ouzou's play.

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:18.030
What's wrong?

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:22.300
You figured all that out and yet you said nothing?

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:25.240
Quite some time has passed since you talked with my father, too.{It's been a while since you talked with my father, too.}

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.370
Why!?

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:29.270
Do I need to say anything?

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:34.480
You said it yourself. Just score. Nothing else matters.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:40.080
I was getting prepared for your lecture.

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:43.320
I was a bit perplexed too.

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:47.230
But I know now. That's just the personalities of you guys.

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:51.330
Isn't that great? Who cares if you're a bit twisted.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:57.070
Not like gentlemen? Perfect! There's no need to beat yourself up over that.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.370
Ryuuji.

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:02.570
Do you like playing soccer?

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:04.510
Yes!

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.940
Me, too.

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:12.350
But I've never seen a player who aims at creating own goals.

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:16.150
I don't really understand it myself. 
I just watch how the opponent moves.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:17.560
And it works?

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:18.690
Yes.

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:22.130
I kick it really fast so they can't react in time.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.860
But your accuracy drops, right?

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:27.470
Not really. I kick it with the inside of my foot.

00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:29.800
You're really something.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.270
One more question.

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:37.380
You keep saying stuff like there's no time left.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.310
Oh, that's because of our parents.

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.510
Your father?{Your parents? }

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:44.820
Not just my father. My mother, too.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:45.920
Your mother?

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:49.920
My mother was the national champion in judo.

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:53.590
My father looks like that but he is renowned internationally.

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:55.760
A judo athlete and a mathematician, huh?

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:58.800
Our parents love us a lot.

00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:01.000
That's great.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.370
My mom wants us to become number one athletes in Japan.

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:08.510
My dad wants us to become famous scholars.

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:12.310
That's quite a lot of pressure.

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:16.810
In any case, I want to become number one in soccer first.

00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:21.690
Coach?

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:25.260
You're great. Just great.

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:29.390
You're the worst, laughing at other people's dreams.

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:33.230
A videotape in this day and age?

00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:33.930
Yeah.

00:22:33.930 --> 00:22:35.330
I got that today.

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:37.340
The Netherlands team with Cruyff!

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:38.470
You know a lot.

00:22:38.470 --> 00:22:40.470
I love Cruyff!

00:22:40.470 --> 00:22:41.540
Ouzou-kun, too!

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:44.040
Take it. Watch it with them.

00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:45.510
Can I?

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:47.040
I told you this before.

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:49.810
Don't aim for something small like becoming Japan's number one.

00:22:49.810 --> 00:22:53.150
If you have the heart for it, then conquer the entire world!

00:22:53.150 --> 00:22:54.320
Yes!

00:22:55.220 --> 00:22:59.020
That's great. These guys are good enough!

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:03.560
I'll conquer the nation with this team!

00:24:35.690 --> 00:24:38.660
Shou-kun, do you know your strong point?

00:24:38.660 --> 00:24:39.760
My voice is loud!

00:24:39.760 --> 00:24:40.990
I'm fast!

00:24:40.990 --> 00:24:42.860
Then my forehead is wide!

00:24:42.860 --> 00:24:44.360
I have a ponytail!

00:24:44.360 --> 00:24:46.230
That's your charm point!

00:24:46.230 --> 00:24:49.700
Thank you very much!

00:24:49.700 --> 00:24:53.200
Next episode of Ginga e Kickoff!! Strong Point!
